{"id":"new-delhi","name":"新德里","en":"New Delhi","country":"","lat":28.614,"lng":77.209,"dek":"一座为统治而生的首都，宽阔、克制、带着旧帝国的尺度。","history":"新德里的历史起点并不古老。1911年12月，英王乔治五世在德里杜尔巴上宣布，将英属印度的首都从加尔各答迁至德里。三天后，他与玛丽王后在金斯威营地为新都奠基。此前，加尔各答已深陷印度独立运动的浪潮，反英情绪与抵制英货行动让殖民政府感到难以继续在那里立足。德里地处印度北方腹地，对殖民政府而言，从这里统治印度更为方便。\n\n这座城市由英国建筑师埃德温·鲁琴斯与赫伯特·贝克规划。鲁琴斯设计中央行政区时，试图以宽阔的放射形大道、对称的政府建筑与巨大圆顶，展现帝国的威仪。修建在一战后真正展开，历时约二十年。1931年2月，印度总督艾文勋爵为新都揭幕。人们后来把这片区域称作“鲁琴斯的德里”。\n\n事实上，德里地区历史上曾出现过八座城。从孔雀帝国时代起，这里就一再成为权力中心。莫卧儿皇帝沙贾汗于1639年兴建了留存至今的旧德里，当时称沙贾汗纳巴德。印度独立后，政府完整保留了旧德里，并以西南方的新德里作为新共和国的首都。新德里由此成为德里的第八座城。","culture":"新德里的文化身份与它的政治功能紧密相连。总统府到印度门之间绵延数公里的宽阔大道，是按阅兵与纪念的尺度设计的。每年1月26日的共和国日游行在这里举行，展现一个有意识构建的国家形象。城市中心以姆拉斯广场为原点，街道呈辐射状伸向四面八方，这种规划本身就带着秩序至上的色彩。\n\n作为首都，新德里容纳着来自印度各地的语言、宗教与饮食习惯。排灯节、侯丽节、开斋节、圣诞节在这里并行不悖。现代地标也延续了这种多元取向：东南部的巴哈伊莲花寺以白色花瓣造型建成，是全世界访客最多的建筑之一；日本佛教组织在城中修建的和平塔，则由达赖喇嘛主持落成。","pull":"一座为统治而生的首都，宽阔、克制、带着旧帝国的尺度。","sights":[{"name":"印度门","orig":"India Gate","intro":"建于1931年，外观借鉴巴黎凯旋门，纪念第一次世界大战和第三次英阿战争中为英军阵亡的约九万名印度士兵。如今拱门内部不再对公众开放，但基座一带仍是新德里最具仪式感的公共空间。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/India_Gate_front.jpg/960px-India_Gate_front.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":1048},"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_Gate"},{"name":"总统府","orig":"Rashtrapati Bhavan","intro":"印度总统官邸，由埃德温·鲁琴斯设计，屋顶为巨大的半球形结构，带有莫卧儿建筑遗风。它与印度门之间由国王大道相连，构成新德里中轴线的西端。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Forecourt%2C_Rashtrapati_Bhavan_-_1.jpg/960px-Forecourt%2C_Rashtrapati_Bhavan_-_1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":640},"src":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%8D%B0%E5%BA%A6%E6%80%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%BA%9C"},{"name":"胡马雍陵","orig":"Humayun's Tomb","intro":"莫卧儿皇帝胡马雍的陵墓，建于16世纪，以红砂岩与白色大理石建造，是印度次大陆最早的波斯式花园陵墓之一。其格局被认为影响了后来的泰姬陵，现列入世界遗产。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Humayun%27s_Tomb_from_the_entrance%2C_Delhi.jpg/960px-Humayun%27s_Tomb_from_the_entrance%2C_Delhi.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":720},"src":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E8%83%A1%E9%A6%AC%E9%9B%8D%E9%99%B5"},{"name":"贾玛清真寺","orig":"Jama Masjid","intro":"17世纪由莫卧儿皇帝沙贾汗兴建，是印度规模最大的清真寺之一。庭院可容纳数万人礼拜，红砂岩与白色大理石的搭配在旧德里天际线上十分醒目。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Jama_Masjid%2C_Facade%2C_Delhi%2C_India.jpg/960px-Jama_Masjid%2C_Facade%2C_Delhi%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":640},"src":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E8%B4%BE%E7%8E%9B%E6%B8%85%E7%9C%9F%E5%AF%BA_(%E5%BE%B7%E9%87%8C)"},{"name":"莲花寺","orig":"Lotus Temple","intro":"巴哈伊信仰的礼拜堂，1986年建成，外形由白色花瓣状结构组成。建筑位于新德里东南部，因造型独特，成为全球参观人数最多的建筑之一。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/LotusDelhi.jpg/960px-LotusDelhi.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":593},"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lotus_Temple"}],"foods":[{"name":"印度烤饼","orig":"Paratha","intro":"一种油煎或干烙的印度面饼，可原味或包入土豆、萝卜、奶酪等馅料。旧德里月光集市的Paranthe Wali Gali以整条街只卖这种饼而闻名。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Triangle_paratha_%28cropped%29.JPG/960px-Triangle_paratha_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":959},"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paratha"},{"name":"甜炸面圈","orig":"Jalebi","intro":"用面粉糊挤成螺旋形后油炸，再浸入糖浆的甜点，外脆内甜。在新德里街头和节庆场合都很常见，常与热奶或酸奶搭配食用。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Basavanagudi_Kadalekai_Parishe_%282025%29_Bangalore_%2886%29.jpg/960px-Basavanagudi_Kadalekai_Parishe_%282025%29_Bangalore_%2886%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":723},"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalebi"},{"name":"印式小食拼盘","orig":"Chaat","intro":"北印度街头小吃的统称，常以炸脆的面壳为底，加入土豆、豆泥、酸奶、酸辣酱和香料粉。新德里是这类食物最集中的城市之一。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Dahi_puri%2C_Doi_phuchka.jpg/960px-Dahi_puri%2C_Doi_phuchka.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":640},"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaat"},{"name":"空心炸球","orig":"Pani puri / Golgappa","intro":"一种小而圆的空心油炸脆球，食用时戳破后填入土豆泥或豆子，再灌入带薄荷与罗望子风味的调味汁。需一口吃下，街头摊点极多。","img":{"u":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pani_Puri1.JPG/960px-Pani_Puri1.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","w":960,"h":636},"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panipuri"}],"hero":[{"u":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/Delhi_Durbar%2C_1911.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","w":1280,"h":712},{"u":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Inauguration_of_New_Delhi_1931.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","w":1280,"h":872}],"outline":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[77.1663519,28.5962391],[77.1681934,28.5911595],[77.1803297,28.5720774],[77.1836175,28.5702471],[77.1888637,28.5696396],[77.1929959,28.5671544],[77.1992662,28.5697816],[77.2007753,28.5625863],[77.2054017,28.5635489],[77.2091027,28.5604008],[77.2108005,28.5631386],[77.2165947,28.5680459],[77.2186608,28.574026],[77.2182206,28.5756432],[77.2143219,28.573245],[77.2093363,28.5732765],[77.2116,28.5800293],[77.224958,28.5795718],[77.2236824,28.5905679],[77.2436519,28.593163],[77.2407234,28.5972171],[77.2399778,28.6098123],[77.2408851,28.6260095],[77.22335,28.6352662],[77.2218319,28.6375685],[77.2205832,28.644735],[77.2180679,28.644325],[77.2184632,28.6419284],[77.2138818,28.6361493],[77.2033625,28.6426773],[77.1973438,28.6451844],[77.1965353,28.6427483],[77.1892949,28.6337051],[77.1868425,28.6291399],[77.1767634,28.6198353],[77.1747332,28.6117287],[77.171607,28.6079905],[77.1670526,28.5993703],[77.1663519,28.5962391]]]},"credit":{"model":"deepseek-v4-pro","wiki":null}}